{
  "dom_id": "step-q111166",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P((X-1)^{2}+{Y}^{2}<1).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,2],$ and the event $A=\\{(X-1)^{2}+{Y}^{2}<1\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below, which is a semicircle of radius $R=1:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14154394/assets/f7f9f016d5f121b2153c1833c959be76f5a11eabb121533dd11839d6da973814.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X-1)^{2}+{Y}^{2}<1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\pi {R}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
